This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:

This session continued from a previous conversation. Three major feature groups were worked on:

**A. Three Messaging UI Improvements** (implementation of features designed in previous session):
1. **Owner Messages Dashboard at `/owner/messages`**: A new global (not per-facility) split-pane page showing all threads across all facilities. Chat header must show player's booking status prominently with color-coded badge — green "Apmokėta" (confirmed), red "Atšaukta" (cancelled), amber "Laukiama" (pending/awaiting). Format: "Arnas | Rezervacija: Gegužės 18, 15:30 (Apmokėta)". Security rationale: prevents giving door codes to people with cancelled bookings.
2. **Game Group Chat System Messages**: Backend injects centered gray pill messages: "Arnas prisijungė prie mačo." on player join, "Mačas pilnas!" or "Mačas pilnas! Laukiama apmokėjimų." when game fills. Frontend renders `senderUserId === "__system__"` as centered gray pill. Non-mine messages show initials avatar + first name beside the bubble.
3. **Player DM Context Card**: When DM initiated from game/court/facility page, inject a pinned info card at the top of the message list saying "[otherUserName] rašo dėl: [context]" with a link.

**B. WebSocket Real-Time QA Protocol** — three tests were analyzed and two bugs were found and fixed:
- Test 1 (Duplicate Messages): PASSES — dedup checks and named handler cleanup already correct
- Test 2 (Room Leak): FAILS/FIXED — no leave_rooms, sockets accumulate in stale game rooms
- Test 3 (Multi-Tab Sync): FAILS/FIXED — reading messages in Tab 1 didn't sync badge to Tab 2

**C. Home Page Performance — 7 fixes in 3 phases**:
- Phase 1: React Query cache optimization (staleTime, remove invalidation effect)
- Phase 2: Backend stats endpoint — 7 sequential DB queries → 2 parallel with conditional aggregation
- Phase 3 (in progress): Lazy-load CourtMap, split vendor chunk, fetchPriority on hero image

---

2. Key Technical Concepts:

- **Socket.IO room lifecycle**: `join_rooms` / `leave_rooms` events; rooms named `dm_${uid1}_${uid2}` (sorted), `game_${gameId}`, `inbox_${userId}`, `facility_${courtId}_${playerId}`
- **System message sentinel**: `senderUserId = "__system__"` in `gameChatTable` to inject automated messages without schema change
- **React Query staleTime**: Setting `staleTime: 300_000` means cached data is valid for 5 minutes — navigating back to home uses the cache instead of refetching
- **`refetchOnMount: "always"` anti-pattern**: Forces a fetch even when fresh cached data exists
- **Conditional SQL aggregation**: `count(*) filter (where column = 'value')` runs multiple count conditions in a single DB pass
- **`Promise.all` for parallel DB queries**: Two parallel queries vs. 7 sequential
- **React.lazy() for named exports**: `lazy(() => import("...").then(m => ({ default: m.NamedExport })))`
- **LCP / fetchpriority**: `fetchPriority="high"` on the first hero image signals it as the Largest Contentful Paint element
- **Vite manualChunks**: Grouping node_modules by concern (maps, ui, auth, query) for parallel download
- **`SPORT_LABELS` canonical source**: `sport-icon.tsx` is the single source of truth; `sportLithuanian` in `court-map.tsx` was a 10-sport subset; replaced with `SPORT_LABELS` (17 sports) + `count > 0` filter on desktop list
- **unread_update socket event**: Emitted from backend to `inbox_${userId}` room to sync badge across all user's tabs

---

3. Files and Code Sections:

**`artifacts/api-server/src/routes/games.ts`** (modified)
- Added `insertSystemMessage` helper at module level (after `toMin` helper):
```typescript
async function insertSystemMessage(gameId: number, body: string): Promise<void> {
  try {
    const [msg] = await db.insert(gameChatTable).values({
      gameId,
      senderUserId: "__system__",
      senderName: "Sistema",
      body,
    }).returning();
    const formatted = { ...msg, createdAt: msg.createdAt.toISOString() };
    socketEmit(`game_${gameId}`, "new_message", { type: "game", message: formatted });
  } catch { /* non-critical */ }
}
```
- In `POST /games/:id/join`, after insert with `newStatus === "joined"`, before the full-check block:
```typescript
// System message: player joined
await insertSystemMessage(id, `${userName} prisijungė prie mačo.`);

// Auto-close if full (only for direct joins)
const [newCountRow] = await db.select(...)...;
if (Number(newCountRow?.count ?? 0) >= g.playersNeeded) {
  await db.update(gamesTable).set({ status: "full" }).where(eq(gamesTable.id, id));
  const fullMsg = g.bookingId ? "Mačas pilnas! Laukiama apmokėjimų." : "Mačas pilnas!";
  await insertSystemMessage(id, fullMsg);
}
```

**`artifacts/courtbook/src/components/chat-bubble.tsx`** (modified)
- `GameChatView` messages renderer — system message branch + sender avatar for non-mine:
```tsx
if (m.senderUserId === "__system__") {
  return (
    <div key={m.id} className="flex justify-center my-1">
      <div className="bg-muted/70 text-muted-foreground text-[11px] px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full border border-border/50">
        {m.body}
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
const isMine = m.senderUserId === user?.id;
const firstName = m.senderName.split(" ")[0];
return (
  <div key={m.id} className={`flex gap-2 ${isMine ? "justify-end" : "justify-start"}`}>
    {!isMine && (
      <div className="flex flex-col items-center gap-0.5 shrink-0 pt-0.5">
        <div className="h-7 w-7 rounded-full bg-primary/15 flex items-center justify-center text-primary font-semibold text-[10px]">
          {m.senderName.split(" ").map(n => n[0]).join("").slice(0, 2).toUpperCase()}
        </div>
        <span className="text-[9px] text-muted-foreground leading-tight">{firstName}</span>
      </div>
    )}
    <div className={`max-w-[72%] rounded-2xl px-3 py-2 ${isMine ? "bg-primary text-primary-foreground rounded-br-md" : "bg-muted rounded-bl-md"}`}>
      ...
    </div>
  </div>
);
```
- `GameChatView` join/leave fix:
```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  const s = getSocket();
  s.emit("join_rooms", { gameId: game.id });
  return () => { s.emit("leave_rooms", { gameId: game.id }); };
}, [game.id]);
```
- `ChatThreadView` DM room join/leave fix:
```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  const s = getSocket();
  s.emit("join_rooms", { dmUserId: otherUserId });
  return () => { s.emit("leave_rooms", { dmUserId: otherUserId }); };
}, [otherUserId]);
```
- `ChatThreadView` context card at top of message list:
```tsx
