5. **Add working hours to court detail page** — parse and render `workingHours` JSON field
6. **Condense working hours into an accordion** — Radix Collapsible, collapsed by default showing only today, dense rows, badge always visible

---

## 2. Key Technical Concepts

- **React.lazy() + Suspense**: Lazy-loading page routes and heavy UI components to reduce initial bundle
- **`lazyPage()` helper**: Factory that wraps a lazy import in its own Suspense so it can be used as a plain Wouter `<Route component={X}>` without per-route Suspense boilerplate
- **Vite manualChunks**: Splitting vendor bundle into logical parallel-downloadable groups: `vendor-maps`, `vendor-auth`, `vendor-query`, `vendor-ui`, `vendor`
- **fetchPriority="high"**: Signals the LCP hero image to the browser preload scanner
- **Progressive hero image loading**: `loadedHeroImages` Set tracks which images have been loaded; initially only 0+1, next image preloaded on each heroIdx change, cross-fade preserved
- **Deferred notification polling**: `setTimeout(..., 2000)` before first `fetchNotifs()` call to avoid competing with critical home page queries
- **Radix UI Collapsible**: `Collapsible`, `CollapsibleTrigger`, `CollapsibleContent` from `@/components/ui/collapsible`
- **workingHours format**: JSON string `Record<"0"|...|"6", { open: string; close: string; closed: boolean }>` where 0=Sunday, 1=Monday, ..., 6=Saturday
- **`(court as any).workingHours`** pattern: Used for fields present in API response but missing from generated `Court` TypeScript interface (same pattern as `hasSmartLock`, `surfaceSpeed`, `surfaceBounce`)
- **`resolveJsonModule: true`** in tsconfig: Enables JSON imports, but only resolves `.json` extension (not `.geojson`)

---

## 3. Files and Code Sections

### `artifacts/courtbook/src/pages/home.tsx`
- **Phase 3 completion**: Wrapped both `<CourtMap>` usages (desktop h-[440px] and mobile 55vh) in `<Suspense fallback={<Skeleton className="w-full h-full rounded-xl" />}>`
- Added `fetchPriority={i === 0 ? "high" : "auto"}` to hero img map
- Added `const [loadedHeroImages, setLoadedHeroImages] = useState(() => new Set([0, 1]));`
- Added preload useEffect after the hero interval useEffect:
```ts
useEffect(() => {
  const nextIdx = (heroIdx + 1) % HERO_IMAGES.length;
  setLoadedHeroImages(prev => {
    if (prev.has(nextIdx)) return prev;
    const s = new Set(prev);
    s.add(nextIdx);
    return s;
  });
}, [heroIdx]);
```
- Hero images map changed to skip unrendered images: `if (!loadedHeroImages.has(i)) return null;`

### `artifacts/courtbook/vite.config.ts`
- Replaced single `"vendor"` chunk with grouped manualChunks:
```ts
manualChunks(id) {
  if (!id.includes("node_modules")) return;
  if (id.includes("@react-google-maps") || id.includes("leaflet") || id.includes("react-leaflet")) return "vendor-maps";
  if (id.includes("@clerk")) return "vendor-auth";
  if (id.includes("@tanstack")) return "vendor-query";
  if (id.includes("@radix-ui") || id.includes("lucide-react")) return "vendor-ui";
  return "vendor";
}
```

### `artifacts/courtbook/src/App.tsx`
- Added `type ComponentType` to React import
- Added `lazyPage()` helper before all page constants:
```ts
function lazyPage(fn: () => Promise<{ default: ComponentType }>) {
  const Comp = lazy(fn);
  function Page() { return <Suspense fallback={null}><Comp /></Suspense>; }
  return Page;
}
```
- Converted all 37 static page imports to `lazyPage(() => import("@/pages/..."))` — variable names identical, all routes unchanged
